":"","content":"<a href=\"https://booklist.werwolf-live.de\" target=\"_blank\">Database</a> updated with <a href=\"https://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=440353&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">W20: Howls of the Apocalypse</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> It is for Backers as of now, so the Link doesn't allow you to buy, yet. But soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T18:27:24-08:00","id":1556326,"title":"","content":"I know this is a dead thread, but I genuinely would sell one of my kidneys to have the &quot;<b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/28/axis-mundi-the-book-of-spirits?products_id=28&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Axis Mundi: Book of Spirits</a></b>&quot; book for Werewolf be print on demand, because of how much it is mandatory reading for new Storytellers.<br /> <br /> Anybody who's trying to get into the setting of Werewolf, absolutely needs this book. I would personally spend more money on a POD of the book than its worth, because not only do I want the physical copy, but also the relief in knowing that any existing copies of this book can be replaced if damaged.<br /> <br /> I probably would not feel as strongly about this book, if I didn't feel as though this book's contents were so important for games of both Werewolf, Mage, and the entire setting in general.<br /> <br /> I want to get more people into the Umbra and metaphysical aspects of the setting, and this book is literally a cornerstone in how a Storyteller incorporates the Umbra (which is a mandatory part of the games' world) into their games!<br /> <br /> If a kickstarter (or anything, really) does come up or any opportunities to get the Axis Mundi book onto Print-on-Demand, please let me know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T01:17:27-08:00","id":1556336,"title":"","content":"I actually do still update the database with new products for W5, V5, and H5 - as well as Chronicles stuff, if I learn about it....<br /> <br /> But yeah, the process of making the backcatalogue available as PoD has somewhat stalled. Also, the printers I got my books from were in the UK, so Brexit made them natably more expensive. <br /> <br /> Right now, my library is still complete with all cWoD books - although it has been boxed up for years now. Didn't unpack after my last move.<br /> <br /> 'Axis Mundi' is a great book. It is not necessarily a must read, in my opinion, and I would dispute some of the information in it, but it makes some great additions to Werewolf's worldbuilding. Other aspects, like the Children of Karnak (if I get it right from the top of my head), are a bit to 'Flash Gordon'-esqu for my opinion, and more suited for Mage (which is fine, since it offitially is a crossover source book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-2